-- חוזר לבעלויות תשס"ז/4 — תשלום בגין שחיקה לעובדי הוראה לשנים 1999–2001 (27.5.2007)
-- Carrying out the arbitration award of 22.5.2007 on the erosion of
-- teachers' pay: a 4.75% rise in the salary table and in the shekel
-- supplements from 1.1.2007, a one-time grant for 1.1.1999–31.12.2001, the
-- budget-pension retirees, and the payment dates.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `תשלום בגין שחיקה לעובדי הוראה לשנים 1999–2001`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, title, date, addressee, subject line, and the recital of the 1.2.2007 agreement that sent the dispute to arbitration and of the award of 22.5.2007; no rule.

-- Time in this file is counted in salary months from May 2007 (0), the
-- circular's own month.
`May 2007 salary`     MEANS 0
`June 2007 salary`    MEANS 1
`July 2007 salary`    MEANS 2
`January 2008 salary` MEANS 8

`the rise`              MEANS 4.75%
`the rise takes effect` MEANS Date 1 1 2007

§§ `1 עדכון טבלת השכר`

-- ¶2: the updated table is "attached as an annex"; the corpus carries no
-- annex (nor does the source PDF), so the table itself is not data here.
@ref akn:art_1/p1 akn:art_1/p2
GIVEN `cell before the update` IS A NUMBER @desc a cell of the salary table as it stood before 1.1.2007
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `updated salary table cell` `cell before the update` IS
    `cell before the update` TIMES (1 PLUS `the rise`)

§§ `2 עדכון תוספות שכר שקליות`

DECLARE `shekel supplement` HAS
    `supplement name`          IS A STRING
    `amount from 1.1.2007`     IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_2/p1
GIVEN `amount before the update` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `updated shekel supplement` `amount before the update` IS
    `amount before the update` TIMES (1 PLUS `the rise`)

@ref akn:art_2__para_a akn:art_2__para_a/p2 akn:art_2__para_b akn:art_2__para_b/p2
`the updated shekel supplements` MEANS
    LIST `shekel supplement` "framework agreement supplement '87" 150.52,
         `shekel supplement` "1994 agreement supplement, reinforced teaching" 135.35

§§ `3 תשלום מענק חד פעמי`

`grant period start` MEANS Date 1 1 1999
`grant period end`   MEANS Date 31 12 2001
`grant rate`         MEANS 3.5%
`advance rate`       MEANS 0.5%

@desc One month in which the teacher was actually employed.
DECLARE `employed month` HAS
    `first day of the month`              IS A DATE
    `salary determining for pension`      IS A NUMBER  @desc the month's salary determining the pension
    `advance paid for the month`          IS A NUMBER  @desc the 0.5% advance already paid for this month (circular תשס"ו/7, which this circular cites); an input

GIVEN m IS AN `employed month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falls in the grant period` m IF
        m's `first day of the month` AT LEAST `grant period start`
    AND m's `first day of the month` AT MOST `grant period end`

-- §3א: 3.5% of the pension-determining salary for each month employed in
-- the period, less the 0.5% advance paid for those months.
@ref akn:art_3__para_a
GIVEN months IS A LIST OF `employed month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the one-time grant` months IS
    sum (map (GIVEN m YIELD `grant rate` TIMES m's `salary determining for pension`
                            MINUS m's `advance paid for the month`)
             (filter `falls in the grant period` months))

DECLARE `erosion action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the grant` HAS `grant paid` IS A NUMBER
    `start the current payments`
    `pay the differences`

@ref akn:art_3__para_b
GIVEN months IS A LIST OF `employed month`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `erosion action`
DECIDE `the grant is paid by January 2008` months IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the grant` amount
          PROVIDED amount AT LEAST `the one-time grant` months
    WITHIN `January 2008 salary`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "§3ב: the grant is paid no later than January 2008's salary"

-- akn:art_3__para_c Detailed instructions for the grant are to be published near its payment date; no rule here.

§§ `4 גמלאים`

-- §4א: §§1–3 apply to budget-pension retirees in proportion to their
-- pension rate.
@ref akn:art_4__para_a
GIVEN `amount for an active teacher` IS A NUMBER
      `pension rate`                 IS A NUMBER @desc the retiree's pension as a share of the salary (e.g. 0.7)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a budget-pension retiree's amount` `amount for an active teacher` `pension rate` IS
    `amount for an active teacher` TIMES `pension rate`

-- §4ב: old-fund retirees who were active in 1999–2001 and retired in
-- 2000–2002 are compensated by the Ministry directly with the funds, not by
-- the owning body.
@ref akn:art_4__para_b
GIVEN `insured in an old pension fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `active in 1999–2001`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `year of retirement`             IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compensated by the Ministry through the old funds` `insured in an old pension fund` `active in 1999–2001` `year of retirement` IF
        `insured in an old pension fund`
    AND `active in 1999–2001`
    AND `year of retirement` AT LEAST 2000
    AND `year of retirement` AT MOST 2002

§§ `5 מועדי התשלום`

@ref akn:art_5__para_a
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `erosion action`
DECIDE `the current payments start by July 2007` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `start the current payments`
    WITHIN `July 2007 salary`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "§5א: the current payments start from May 2007's salary and no later than July 2007's"

@ref akn:art_5__para_b
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `erosion action`
DECIDE `the differences are paid by July 2007` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the differences`
    WITHIN `July 2007 salary`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "§5ב: the differences are paid in June 2007's salary and at the latest July 2007's"

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and signature; no rule.

-- Examples. Salaries of 10,000 and the advances are placeholders.
`three months of 2001 and one of 2002` MEANS
    LIST `employed month` (Date 1 10 2001) 10000 50,
         `employed month` (Date 1 11 2001) 10000 50,
         `employed month` (Date 1 12 2001) 10000 50,
         `employed month` (Date 1 1 2002) 10000 50

#ASSERT `the one-time grant` `three months of 2001 and one of 2002` EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `updated salary table cell` 1000 EQUALS 1047.5
#ASSERT `a budget-pension retiree's amount` 900 0.7 EQUALS 630
#ASSERT `compensated by the Ministry through the old funds` TRUE TRUE 2001

#TRACE `the grant is paid by January 2008` `three months of 2001 and one of 2002` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the grant` 900 AT 8
#TRACE `the current payments start by July 2007` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `start the current payments` AT 0
#TRACE `the differences are paid by July 2007` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the differences` AT 1
